# Every text file is LF in the repository, whatever a checkout does on the working copy.
# Without this a fresh clone on Windows turned hundreds of tests red at once: the suites read
# source and markup files byte for byte, and a CRLF working-tree copy does not match what
# they assert. The index has always stored LF; this is the line that says so out loud.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Second line of defence, for a checkout made before that line existed or a file an editor
# rewrote in passing: server/test/lib/read-source.mjs folds CRLF to LF on the way in, so
# every suite here reads the same bytes whatever is on disk. This line is still the one
# that matters — it is what keeps the working copy and the index identical — but a test
# about markup should not be able to fail over line endings even when it has been undone.

# Binaries git must never inspect for line endings, let alone rewrite.
*.woff2 -text
*.woff -text
*.ttf -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.webp -text
*.gif -text
*.ico -text
